Explanation:
- Motor interacts with Gearbox (to transmit power), Chuck (through the gearbox and transmission), Handle (for physical support), Battery (power source) and Switch (to start/stop).
- Gearbox interacts with Motor (receives power from it) and Chuck (transmits motion to it).
- Chuck interacts with Gearbox (receives motion from it) and Handle (for physical support).
- Handle only supports other components physically.
- Battery provides power to the Motor and is controlled by Switch.
- Switch controls the operation of Motor and Battery.
- Transmission connects Motor to Chuck through Gearbox, but doesn't directly interact with any other component in this context.
