- The Clutch interacts with the Gearbox (receives adjusted power from it) and Chuck (drives it based on clutch engagement).
- The Chuck interacts with the Motor (driven by it), Clutch (driven by it when engaged), and Trigger (speed of rotation controlled by it).
- The Trigger interacts with the Motor (controls its operation and speed), and Handle (operated by user's hand on handle).
- The Battery or Power Cord interacts only with the Motor, providing energy to it.
- The Handle interacts with the Trigger (part of the same assembly) and Motor (indirectly through trigger operation).
