- The Gearbox reduces motor speed and increases torque before transmitting it to the Chuck.
- The Chuck holds the screwdriver bit and is driven by the Gearbox.
- The Handle provides a grip for the user and houses other components like the Motor, Battery, Switch, etc. It may also interact with the Torque Adjustment component if present.
- The Battery supplies power to the Motor through the Switch.
